Z||000000||Rare87GT||12-24-2001||04:20 PM||||I know the Pro Kit lowers your car .8" and the Sportline Kit lowers it about 1.5" I think if I am right.  Just wondering where to find the Sportline Kit, and if I lowered it with Eibach's would I need camber plates.  Just wondering from the people that have bought Eibach's.  Let me know what Kit you have for your car.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>1987 GT (Maroon)*5 Speed*<BR>(Canadian Car)<BR>2.8L Mods--No Cat, K&N||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||12-24-2001||04:31 PM||||The Eibach springs I have I think were called "Pro" and they lowered the car by 1.5" I thought the Sportslines were the .8"<BR>As for camber adjustment, Just get the MOOG "Problem Solver" Upper ball joints. These aloow a wide range of camber adjustment and some slight caster adjustment.<P>You can check with "Tire Rack" they had all 3 versions of the Eibach's .8" 1.5" and the 2". Their prices were not bad and delivery is fast.<P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rare87GT||12-24-2001||04:44 PM||||The only one I see on tirerack.com is the one that lowers it .8".  Go check and see Oreif, but that's the only one I see there.  ||||reg||1
